  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposal is unacceptable in principle as it results in\r\nthe loss of larger family dwelling house and replaced with smaller flatted\r\ndevelopment. The proposal fails to satisfy the requirements of Policy 20 (Housing\r\nin Multiple Occupation and Conversions) of the adopted Local Plan (2024).",
    "The overall development would not satisfy minimum internal\r\nspace standards in accordance with Policy D6 of the London Plan (2021), and\r\nPolicy 56 (Residential Space Standards) of the adopted Local Plan (2024).",
    "The proposed development, fails to make adequate provision\r\nfor secure storage of 5No. bicycles, contrary to Policy T5 of the London Plan,\r\nPolicy 61 (Active Travel)&nbsp;and Appendix 1 – Parking standards of\r\nthe&nbsp;Local Plan (2024) and London Cycle Design Standards (2014).",
    "The applicant has failed to enter into a S106 agreement and\r\ntherefore not in compliance with Policy 94 (Infrastructure and Developer\r\nContributions) of the adopted Local Plan (2024).\r\n\r\n\r\n A&nbsp;S106\r\n     request of £2,000 is requested toward improving sustainable modes of\r\n     transport including walking and cycling in the sites vicinity which will\r\n     directly benefit new residents in this car free development.\r\n The site\r\n     is within a CPZ and therefore the additional unit must be classified as\r\n     car free for future residents not being entitled to parking permits. \r\n If minded for approval S278 works will be required. Upon completion\r\n     of the works relating to the development prior to occupation.&nbsp;Works\r\n     will include but are not limited to: \r\n \r\n  Renewal of footway fronting the entire development.\r\n  At the frontage of the site the road markings are to be refreshed.\r\n  \r\n   The highways department will need to be contacted for an\r\n       application form for developer highway works. The application will need\r\n       to accompany a plan to be submitted for approval and estimate. Works\r\n       will be carried out by the Council and funded by the developer.\r\n  \r\n \r\n Financial contribution of £1254 towards Strategic\r\n     Access Management and Monitoring Strategies (SAMMS) against mitigating the\r\n     impact of the development upon the Epping Forest Special Area of\r\n     Conservation (SAC).\r\n"
  ],
